('606c7c81-67c3-5e7f-bedd-ad57c7f58d85','03b35ba8-9bd6-55b0-9b2c-bd7b0500db76',1,'how old','چند ساله','spoken & written','the number of years someone has lived or something has existed','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'سن، عمر؛ عصر، دوره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['old age (= the time when you are old ) the problems of old age','middle age (= between about 40 and 60 ) He was in late middle age.','a great/advanced age (= a very old age ) My aunt died at a great age. Kirby is not alone in wanting to run his own business at an advanced age.','a difficult/awkward age (= used mainly about the time when people are teenagers ) 13 – 16 is often a difficult age.','retirement age The risk of experiencing poverty is much greater for those over retirement age.','school age Children should start doing homework as they approach high school age.','school-leaving age British English The government is proposing to raise the minimum school-leaving age.','the legal age In the US, the legal age for drinking alcohol is 21.','the minimum age 16 years is the minimum age to drive a car.','the voting age plans to bring down the voting age from 18 to 16','the marrying age She was 28 – long past the usual marrying age.','from an early/young age She’d been playing the piano from a very early age.','at an early/young age Kids can start learning a second language at a young age.','somebody (of) your own age He needs to find people his own age.','of childbearing age (= at the age when a woman can have children ) It is against the law to refuse to employ a woman of childbearing age because she may become pregnant.','of working age 55 percent of the people are of working age.','the age of consent (= when you are legally allowed to marry or have sex ) At 15, the girl was under the age of consent.','an age group/bracket/range Men in the 50–65 age group are most at risk from heart disease. The school takes in children from the seven to eleven age range.','an age limit There’s no upper age limit for drivers.','age discrimination laws against age discrimination in the workplace','get to/reach/live to a particular age One in three children here die before they reach the age of 5. The number of people living to to the age of 80 has doubled in the last fifty years.','lower/raise the age (= at which something can be done ) The voting age was lowered from 21 to 18.','look/feel your age (= look or feel as old as you really are ) The singer is 46, but she doesn’t look her age at all. I keep getting aches in my legs and I’m starting to feel my age.','act your age (= behave in the way that a person of your age should behave ) It’s time he started acting his age.','ask/say your age (= ask or say how old you are ) It’s rude to ask a woman her age.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Francis is the same age as me.","translation":"فرانسیس هم سن من است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000976050.mp3"},{"sentence":"Experts disagree over the age of the drawings.","translation":"کارشناسان در مورد قدمت نقاشی ها اختلاف نظر دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001650423.mp3"},{"sentence":"Dad retired at the age of 56.","translation":"پدر در سن 56 سالگی بازنشسته شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001650424.mp3"},{"sentence":"In Britain, schooling starts at age 5.","translation":"در بریتانیا، تحصیل در مدرسه از سن 5 سالگی شروع می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000976064.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was just over 16 years of age.","translation":"او کمی بیشتر از 16 سال سن داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000976060.mp3"},{"sentence":"At my age, it’s quite difficult getting up the stairs.","translation":"در سن من، بالا رفتن از پله ها بسیار سخت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000041.mp3"},{"sentence":"people over the age of 65","translation":"افراد بالای 65 سال","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001650430.mp3"},{"sentence":"She’s tall for her age, isn’t she?","translation":"او نسبت به سنش قد بلندی دارد، اینطور نیست؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000976079.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
('37f1358d-35b3-5a2a-ba73-15354ea7c9fb','03b35ba8-9bd6-55b0-9b2c-bd7b0500db76',2,'legal age','سن قانونی','spoken & written','the age when you are legally old enough to do something','[ uncountable ]',null,'سنی که از نظر قانونی به سن کافی برای انجام کاری رسیده اید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['old age (= the time when you are old ) the problems of old age','middle age (= between about 40 and 60 ) He was in late middle age.','a great/advanced age (= a very old age ) My aunt died at a great age. Kirby is not alone in wanting to run his own business at an advanced age.','a difficult/awkward age (= used mainly about the time when people are teenagers ) 13 – 16 is often a difficult age.','retirement age The risk of experiencing poverty is much greater for those over retirement age.','school age Children should start doing homework as they approach high school age.','school-leaving age British English The government is proposing to raise the minimum school-leaving age.','the legal age In the US, the legal age for drinking alcohol is 21.','the minimum age 16 years is the minimum age to drive a car.','the voting age plans to bring down the voting age from 18 to 16','the marrying age She was 28 – long past the usual marrying age.','from an early/young age She’d been playing the piano from a very early age.','at an early/young age Kids can start learning a second language at a young age.','somebody (of) your own age He needs to find people his own age.','of childbearing age (= at the age when a woman can have children ) It is against the law to refuse to employ a woman of childbearing age because she may become pregnant.','of working age 55 percent of the people are of working age.','the age of consent (= when you are legally allowed to marry or have sex ) At 15, the girl was under the age of consent.','an age group/bracket/range Men in the 50–65 age group are most at risk from heart disease. The school takes in children from the seven to eleven age range.','an age limit There’s no upper age limit for drivers.','age discrimination laws against age discrimination in the workplace','get to/reach/live to a particular age One in three children here die before they reach the age of 5. The number of people living to to the age of 80 has doubled in the last fifty years.','lower/raise the age (= at which something can be done ) The voting age was lowered from 21 to 18.','look/feel your age (= look or feel as old as you really are ) The singer is 46, but she doesn’t look her age at all. I keep getting aches in my legs and I’m starting to feel my age.','act your age (= behave in the way that a person of your age should behave ) It’s time he started acting his age.','ask/say your age (= ask or say how old you are ) It’s rude to ask a woman her age.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"What’s the minimum age for getting a driver’s license?","translation":"حداقل سن برای گرفتن گواهینامه رانندگی چقدر است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000976089.mp3"},{"sentence":"You’re not allowed to buy alcohol. You’re under age (= too young by law ) .","translation":"شما مجاز به خرید الکل نیستید. شما زیر سن هستید (= طبق قانون خیلی جوان هستید).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001650450.mp3"},{"sentence":"The normal retirement age is 65.","translation":"سن عادی بازنشستگی 65 سال است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000042.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('5b4f64d3-2837-5fe5-948b-5848dbfec854','03b35ba8-9bd6-55b0-9b2c-bd7b0500db76',3,'period of life','دوره زندگی','spoken & written','one of the particular periods of someone’s life','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'یکی از دوره های خاص زندگی یک نفر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['old age (= the time when you are old ) the problems of old age','middle age (= between about 40 and 60 ) He was in late middle age.','a great/advanced age (= a very old age ) My aunt died at a great age. Kirby is not alone in wanting to run his own business at an advanced age.','a difficult/awkward age (= used mainly about the time when people are teenagers ) 13 – 16 is often a difficult age.','retirement age The risk of experiencing poverty is much greater for those over retirement age.','school age Children should start doing homework as they approach high school age.','school-leaving age British English The government is proposing to raise the minimum school-leaving age.','the legal age In the US, the legal age for drinking alcohol is 21.','the minimum age 16 years is the minimum age to drive a car.','the voting age plans to bring down the voting age from 18 to 16','the marrying age She was 28 – long past the usual marrying age.','from an early/young age She’d been playing the piano from a very early age.','at an early/young age Kids can start learning a second language at a young age.','somebody (of) your own age He needs to find people his own age.','of childbearing age (= at the age when a woman can have children ) It is against the law to refuse to employ a woman of childbearing age because she may become pregnant.','of working age 55 percent of the people are of working age.','the age of consent (= when you are legally allowed to marry or have sex ) At 15, the girl was under the age of consent.','an age group/bracket/range Men in the 50–65 age group are most at risk from heart disease. The school takes in children from the seven to eleven age range.','an age limit There’s no upper age limit for drivers.','age discrimination laws against age discrimination in the workplace','get to/reach/live to a particular age One in three children here die before they reach the age of 5. The number of people living to to the age of 80 has doubled in the last fifty years.','lower/raise the age (= at which something can be done ) The voting age was lowered from 21 to 18.','look/feel your age (= look or feel as old as you really are ) The singer is 46, but she doesn’t look her age at all. I keep getting aches in my legs and I’m starting to feel my age.','act your age (= behave in the way that a person of your age should behave ) It’s time he started acting his age.','ask/say your age (= ask or say how old you are ) It’s rude to ask a woman her age.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"When you get to old age, everything seems to take longer.","translation":"وقتی به سن پیری می‌رسی، به نظر می‌رسد همه چیز بیشتر طول می‌کشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000043.mp3"},{"sentence":"The early teens are often a difficult age.","translation":"اوایل نوجوانی اغلب سن دشواری دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001650462.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('99a1fd2b-f0af-51d7-bb74-9003960bac62','03b35ba8-9bd6-55b0-9b2c-bd7b0500db76',4,'being old','پیر بودن','spoken & written','the state of being old','[ uncountable ]',null,'حالت پیر بودن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"High blood pressure increases with age.","translation":"فشار خون بالا با افزایش سن افزایش می یابد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000976121.mp3"},{"sentence":"Some of the furniture was showing signs of age .","translation":"برخی از اثاثیه ها نشان از سن داشتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000976122.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('fdd4c1cb-7568-5ff4-b2d9-82c8e6fd372f','03b35ba8-9bd6-55b0-9b2c-bd7b0500db76',5,'period of history','دوره تاریخ','spoken & written','a particular period of history','[ countable usually singular ]','in this day and age ( 6 )','یک دوره خاص از تاریخ',array['era']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We are living in the age of technology.","translation":"ما در عصر تکنولوژی زندگی می کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000976131.mp3"},{"sentence":"Molecular biology is pushing medicine into a new age.","translation":"زیست شناسی مولکولی پزشکی را به عصر جدیدی سوق می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000976130.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c75a4404-b313-562c-ae2a-86f1085e075e','03b35ba8-9bd6-55b0-9b2c-bd7b0500db76',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'ages','سن، عمر؛ عصر، دوره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
