('91ec9226-3cc4-534b-b06b-c5ea850908d5','d6c42292-0ad6-5f44-932a-f70011faacf1',5,'phrase','عبارت','spoken & written','a phrase that is used to unite people in support of a particular action or idea','[ countable ]','battle cry ( 1 ) , war cry','عبارتی که برای متحد کردن مردم در حمایت از یک عمل یا ایده خاص استفاده می شود',array['slogan']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a cry of pain/despair/delight etc A rock was loose and he fell with a sharp cry of surprise.','a cry escapes somebody/sb’s lips A cry escaped her lips as he tightened his grip on her wrist.','give a cry The woman looked up and gave a cry of fear.','let out/utter a cry Seeing the fields and mountains, she let out a cry of delight.','a small/little cry The child gave a small cry and burst into tears.','a loud cry a loud cry of pain','a great cry literary (= a loud cry ) With a great cry they charged into battle.','a sharp cry (= loud, short, and sudden ) He gave a sharp cry of pain.','a low cry (= not loud or high ) I heard a long, low cry of despair.','a strangled/stifled cry (= that stops before it is finished ) The girl gave a stifled cry of disappointment.','a muffled cry (= that cannot be heard clearly ) I thought I heard a muffled cry from somewhere in the building.','an anguished/agonised cry (= full of distress ) She gave an anguished cry, calling his name.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘Land and Liberty’ was the rallying cry of revolutionary Mexico.","translation":"\"سرزمین و آزادی\" فریاد تجمع مکزیک انقلابی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001772823.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7352d78e-bbe5-5668-8a59-16b1038d664a','d6c42292-0ad6-5f44-932a-f70011faacf1',6,'animal/bird','حیوان/پرنده','spoken & written','a sound made by a particular animal','[ countable ]',null,'صدایی که توسط یک حیوان خاص ایجاد می شود',array['call']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a cry of pain/despair/delight etc A rock was loose and he fell with a sharp cry of surprise.','a cry escapes somebody/sb’s lips A cry escaped her lips as he tightened his grip on her wrist.','give a cry The woman looked up and gave a cry of fear.','let out/utter a cry Seeing the fields and mountains, she let out a cry of delight.','a small/little cry The child gave a small cry and burst into tears.','a loud cry a loud cry of pain','a great cry literary (= a loud cry ) With a great cry they charged into battle.','a sharp cry (= loud, short, and sudden ) He gave a sharp cry of pain.','a low cry (= not loud or high ) I heard a long, low cry of despair.','a strangled/stifled cry (= that stops before it is finished ) The girl gave a stifled cry of disappointment.','a muffled cry (= that cannot be heard clearly ) I thought I heard a muffled cry from somewhere in the building.','an anguished/agonised cry (= full of distress ) She gave an anguished cry, calling his name.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the cries of seagulls overhead","translation":"فریاد مرغان دریایی بالای سر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001122145.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('280be184-0721-567f-9e84-56ab8687a9ce','ba0ffc38-4458-5bca-87a8-e02f3ed9353b',1,'for drinking','برای نوشیدن','spoken & written','a small round container , usually with a handle , that you use to drink tea , coffee etc','[ countable ]',null,'فنجان، پیاله؛ جام (قهرمانی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['full The cup was full of hot tea.','empty A girl was clearing away the empty cups.','a paper/plastic/china cup (= one made of paper etc ) All they had to drink was warm beer in plastic cups.','a coffee cup He picked up the coffee cups and took them into the kitchen.','a tea cup ( also teacup ) Mum put a tea cup and saucer on the table.','fill a cup Angie filled the cup and handed it to him.','drain/empty a cup (= drink all the coffee, tea etc in it ) He lifted his cup of coffee and drained it.','a cup and saucer Do you prefer a mug or a cup and saucer?','a set of cups a set of beautiful blue coffee cups']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Mathew picked up the cup and sipped his coffee.","translation":"متیو فنجان را برداشت و قهوه اش را نوشید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748793.mp3"},{"sentence":"She put her cup and saucer down on the table.","translation":"فنجان و نعلبکی اش را روی میز گذاشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001122590.mp3"},{"sentence":"Helen took the coffee cups into the kitchen.","translation":"هلن فنجان های قهوه را به آشپزخانه برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001122593.mp3"},{"sentence":"They drank cheap wine from plastic cups.","translation":"از لیوان های پلاستیکی شراب ارزان می نوشیدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748799.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('cbda8c75-8c5c-5916-9566-be344393bcdc','ba0ffc38-4458-5bca-87a8-e02f3ed9353b',2,'drink','نوشیدنی','spoken & written','the liquid contained inside a cup','[ countable ]',null,'مایع موجود در یک فنجان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['full The cup was full of hot tea.','empty A girl was clearing away the empty cups.','a paper/plastic/china cup (= one made of paper etc ) All they had to drink was warm beer in plastic cups.','a coffee cup He picked up the coffee cups and took them into the kitchen.','a tea cup ( also teacup ) Mum put a tea cup and saucer on the table.','fill a cup Angie filled the cup and handed it to him.','drain/empty a cup (= drink all the coffee, tea etc in it ) He lifted his cup of coffee and drained it.','a cup and saucer Do you prefer a mug or a cup and saucer?','a set of cups a set of beautiful blue coffee cups']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Let’s go and have a cup of coffee.","translation":"بیا بریم یه فنجان قهوه بخوریم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001122609.mp3"},{"sentence":"Will you stay for a cup of tea?","translation":"آیا برای یک فنجان چای می مانی؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001748802.mp3"},{"sentence":"Would you like another cup?","translation":"آیا شما یک فنجان دیگر می خواهید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001122606.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
