('4c80103d-a0eb-5ac0-8ccf-07e4f6966a7b','6a00c2ed-b51a-5b1f-9103-9a4b5ffbdc61',1,'food','غذا','spoken & written','to put food in your mouth and chew and swallow it','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'خوردن، تناول کردن؛ فرسودن (سرمایه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['eat breakfast/lunch/dinner etc What time do you usually eat lunch?','eat well (= have enough food, or have good food ) The people work hard, but they eat well.','eat healthily/sensibly (= eat food that will keep you healthy ) If you eat healthily and exercise regularly, you’ll look and feel a lot better.','eat properly British English , eat right American English (= eat food that will keep you healthy ) He hadn’t been eating properly and was drinking far too much.','eat hungrily (= eat a lot quickly, because you are very hungry ) The children ate hungrily, devouring everything on their plate.','eat sparingly (= eat very little ) Carter joined us for lunch, but ate sparingly, as he always did.','have something/nothing to eat (= eat something/nothing ) We’ll leave after we’ve had something to eat.','have enough/plenty etc to eat Have you had enough to eat?','have little to eat (= not have enough food ) The refugees had very little to eat and no clean water.','find something to eat I got dressed and went downstairs to find something to eat.','get something to eat (= prepare or buy some food ) I’m sure you can get something to eat on the train.','somebody’s eating habits (= the kinds of things they eat or drink regularly ) The doctor asked me about my eating habits and how much I smoked.','an eating disorder (= a mental illness which causes you to eat too much or too little ) She described her battle with the eating disorder bulimia.','a bite to eat (= a small meal ) We should have time for a bite to eat before we set out.','eat like a horse (= eat a lot ) She eats like a horse but never puts on any weight!','eat like a bird (= eat very little ) Ever since she was a child, Jan had always eaten like a bird.','I couldn’t eat another thing spoken (= used to say that you are completely full ) Thanks, that was lovely, but I couldn’t eat another thing.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Felix chatted cheerfully as he ate.","translation":"فلیکس در حالی که غذا می خورد با خوشحالی گپ می زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985286.mp3"},{"sentence":"A small girl was eating an ice cream.","translation":"دختر کوچکی داشت بستنی می خورد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985287.mp3"},{"sentence":"We had plenty to eat and drink.","translation":"ما برای خوردن و نوشیدن زیاد داشتیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985288.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s important to eat healthily when you are pregnant.","translation":"مهم است که در دوران بارداری سالم غذا بخورید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985289.mp3"},{"sentence":"I exercise and eat right and get plenty of sleep.","translation":"من ورزش می کنم و درست غذا می خورم و به اندازه کافی می خوابم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985293.mp3"},{"sentence":"Would you like something to eat ?","translation":"چیزی برای خوردن دوست داری؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985297.mp3"},{"sentence":"She can eat like a horse and never put on weight.","translation":"او می تواند مانند یک اسب غذا بخورد و هرگز چاق نشود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985301.mp3"},{"sentence":"We stopped at McDonalds to get a bite to eat .","translation":"ما در مک دونالد توقف کردیم تا لقمه ای بخوریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985305.mp3"},{"sentence":"Good eating habits are the best way of preventing infection.","translation":"عادات غذایی خوب بهترین راه برای پیشگیری از عفونت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985309.mp3"},{"sentence":"ready-to-eat foods such as deli meats and cheeses","translation":"غذاهای آماده مانند گوشت و پنیر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985313.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘More cake?’ ‘No thanks, I couldn’t eat another thing .’","translation":"«کیک بیشتر؟» «نه ممنون، نمی‌توانستم چیز دیگری بخورم.»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985316.mp3"},{"sentence":"No chicken for me. I don’t eat meat (= I never eat meat ) .","translation":"برای من مرغ نیست من گوشت نمی خورم (= هرگز گوشت نمی خورم) .","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985320.mp3"},{"sentence":"Does Rob eat fish?","translation":"آیا راب ماهی می خورد؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001985323.mp3"}]'::jsonb,13),
('b38429d9-0b66-595b-aa28-65a6f72f364b','6a00c2ed-b51a-5b1f-9103-9a4b5ffbdc61',2,'meal','وعده غذایی','spoken & written','to have a meal','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'برای خوردن یک وعده غذایی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['eat breakfast/lunch/dinner etc What time do you usually eat lunch?','eat well (= have enough food, or have good food ) The people work hard, but they eat well.','eat healthily/sensibly (= eat food that will keep you healthy ) If you eat healthily and exercise regularly, you’ll look and feel a lot better.','eat properly British English , eat right American English (= eat food that will keep you healthy ) He hadn’t been eating properly and was drinking far too much.','eat hungrily (= eat a lot quickly, because you are very hungry ) The children ate hungrily, devouring everything on their plate.','eat sparingly (= eat very little ) Carter joined us for lunch, but ate sparingly, as he always did.','have something/nothing to eat (= eat something/nothing ) We’ll leave after we’ve had something to eat.','have enough/plenty etc to eat Have you had enough to eat?','have little to eat (= not have enough food ) The refugees had very little to eat and no clean water.','find something to eat I got dressed and went downstairs to find something to eat.','get something to eat (= prepare or buy some food ) I’m sure you can get something to eat on the train.','somebody’s eating habits (= the kinds of things they eat or drink regularly ) The doctor asked me about my eating habits and how much I smoked.','an eating disorder (= a mental illness which causes you to eat too much or too little ) She described her battle with the eating disorder bulimia.','a bite to eat (= a small meal ) We should have time for a bite to eat before we set out.','eat like a horse (= eat a lot ) She eats like a horse but never puts on any weight!','eat like a bird (= eat very little ) Ever since she was a child, Jan had always eaten like a bird.','I couldn’t eat another thing spoken (= used to say that you are completely full ) Thanks, that was lovely, but I couldn’t eat another thing.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Let’s eat first and then go to a movie.","translation":"بیا اول بخوریم بعد بریم سینما.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001178927.mp3"},{"sentence":"They’re eating breakfast.","translation":"دارند صبحانه می خورند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-002087116.mp3"},{"sentence":"We could not afford to eat at Walker’s very often.","translation":"ما نمی توانستیم اغلب در Walker’s غذا بخوریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001641371.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
