('c30fd034-a4d4-517d-ba13-bb2b44c58e40','20e24791-8e76-585b-bbdb-13dd4a2097d9',1,'system of rules','سیستم قوانین','spoken & written','the whole system of rules that people in a particular country or area must obey','[ uncountable ]',null,'قانون؛ حقوق (علم)؛ قوانین (حاکم)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['obey the law Citizens have a duty to obey the law.','break the law (= do something illegal ) Is the company breaking the law?','pass a law New Jersey passed a law requiring helmets for scooter riders.','become law (= officially be made a law ) For a bill to become law, it must be approved by both Houses of Parliament.','make laws Part of the function of Parliament is to make laws.','introduce a law In 1989, a new law was introduced to protect the Polish language.','enforce a law (= make people obey a law ) It is the job of the police to enforce the law.','flout a law (= deliberately disobey a law ) Employers who flout the law should be properly punished.','repeal a law (= officially end a law ) Many people want the law to be repealed.','a law prohibits something (= says that it is not allowed ) The law prohibits possession of these animals.','something is against the law (= it is illegal ) The children knew that shoplifting was against the law.','stay/act within the law (= not do illegal things ) The security forces must act within the law.','strict/tough the country’s strict anti-tobacco laws','tax/copyright/divorce etc law(s) an accountant who knows about tax law','criminal law (= laws concerning crimes ) Criminal law contains definitions of such crimes as murder, rape, and robbery.','civil law (= laws concerning disagreements between people, rather than crimes ) The punishment for breaking civil law is usually a fine.','international law (= laws that all countries agree to obey ) Under international law, the countries must respect the treaty.','English/German etc law This is not an offence under English law.','federal law (= the law of the US, not a particular state ) Under federal law, it is illegal to discriminate against employees because of race or sex.','state law (= the law in a US state ) Under state law it was illegal for any public official to receive gifts worth more than $100.','common law (= laws that have come from customs and the decisions of judges ) In common law, if a house is rented out, it is expected that the house is safe to live in.','case law (= law based on previous court cases ) There is little case law covering this issue.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Elected officials ought to obey the law.","translation":"مقامات منتخب باید از قانون پیروی کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001972331.mp3"},{"sentence":"By law, seat belts must be worn by all passengers.","translation":"طبق قانون، کمربند ایمنی برای همه مسافران باید بسته شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001483605.mp3"},{"sentence":"This is illegal under English law.","translation":"این کار طبق قوانین انگلیس غیرقانونی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000924.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('223de78c-b1da-5b3d-8a4b-7219cee21259','20e24791-8e76-585b-bbdb-13dd4a2097d9',2,'a rule','یک قانون','spoken & written','a rule that people in a particular country or area must obey','[ countable ]',null,'قانونی که مردم در یک کشور یا منطقه خاص باید از آن پیروی کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['obey the law Citizens have a duty to obey the law.','break the law (= do something illegal ) Is the company breaking the law?','pass a law New Jersey passed a law requiring helmets for scooter riders.','become law (= officially be made a law ) For a bill to become law, it must be approved by both Houses of Parliament.','make laws Part of the function of Parliament is to make laws.','introduce a law In 1989, a new law was introduced to protect the Polish language.','enforce a law (= make people obey a law ) It is the job of the police to enforce the law.','flout a law (= deliberately disobey a law ) Employers who flout the law should be properly punished.','repeal a law (= officially end a law ) Many people want the law to be repealed.','a law prohibits something (= says that it is not allowed ) The law prohibits possession of these animals.','something is against the law (= it is illegal ) The children knew that shoplifting was against the law.','stay/act within the law (= not do illegal things ) The security forces must act within the law.','strict/tough the country’s strict anti-tobacco laws','tax/copyright/divorce etc law(s) an accountant who knows about tax law','criminal law (= laws concerning crimes ) Criminal law contains definitions of such crimes as murder, rape, and robbery.','civil law (= laws concerning disagreements between people, rather than crimes ) The punishment for breaking civil law is usually a fine.','international law (= laws that all countries agree to obey ) Under international law, the countries must respect the treaty.','English/German etc law This is not an offence under English law.','federal law (= the law of the US, not a particular state ) Under federal law, it is illegal to discriminate against employees because of race or sex.','state law (= the law in a US state ) Under state law it was illegal for any public official to receive gifts worth more than $100.','common law (= laws that have come from customs and the decisions of judges ) In common law, if a house is rented out, it is expected that the house is safe to live in.','case law (= law based on previous court cases ) There is little case law covering this issue.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"laws passed by Parliament","translation":"قوانین مصوب مجلس","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001735761.mp3"},{"sentence":"Five people arrested under anti-terrorism laws were released without charge.","translation":"پنج نفر که بر اساس قوانین ضد تروریسم دستگیر شده بودند، بدون اتهام آزاد شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001735759.mp3"},{"sentence":"European laws on equal opportunities","translation":"قوانین اروپا در مورد فرصت های برابر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001483629.mp3"},{"sentence":"The laws against drug use were very strict.","translation":"قوانین منع مصرف مواد مخدر بسیار سختگیرانه بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000925.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
